The buffer is exactly full -- `StringBytes == NumBytes`, which is how any caller that
pads its own records calls `parse_json` -- and its last byte is a digit.

A digit legally STARTS a number, so the scan stops inside one, in a perfectly legal small
mode. No error state is ever produced. The only thing that noticed was an assert inside
the unconstrained `__build_transcript`, and an assert in an unconstrained function is not
a constraint: a prover who does not want it does not run it. The trailing byte is dropped
and the record is accepted as valid JSON.

The patch removes that assert, which is what "the hint is not a constraint" means in
practice.
